  "text": "2021B12 Describe the effects of perioperative hypothermia. DO\nNOT discuss mechanisms of heat loss.\nHypothermia: core temp\n<36\n°C\nDirect effects:\nMetabolic rate\n·\n↓temp 1\n°\nC = ↓metabolic\nrate 7%\no\n↓Rate of enzymatic reactions\no\n↓ATP hydrolysis\no\n↓Oxidative phosphorylation\no\n↓Krebs cycle activity\no\n↓Glycolysis (-> hyperglycaemia)\no\n↓Drug metabolism (e.g. Hofmann degradation of\ncisatracurium)\nAcid-base\n·\n↑pH 0.015 per 1\n°\nC (Rosenthal equation).\nMultiple factors:\no\n↓Water dissociation into H\n+\nand\nOH\n-\no\n↓Metabolic rate ->\n↓VCO\n2\no\n↑CO\n2\nsolubility ->\n↓partial pressure\n·\nN.B. ↑pH\n∝\n↑pH of ICF\n∝\npH of neutrality\no\nFavours alpha stat management: i.e. allow pH to\nincrease\n§\nOptimal acid-base buffering in ICF\n§\nTrapping of metabolic intermediates in ICF\n§\nPreserved function of enzymes and ion channels\n§\nPreserved CBF autoregulation\no\nAlternative: pH stat management\n§\nLuxury cerebral perfusion\n§\nRapid homogenous cooling\nCardiovascular\n·\nElectrical:\no\nSlowed conduction: bradycardia, prolonged QT, (J\nwave)\no\nArrhythmias: AF, VF (arrest at 28\n°\nC)\no\nResistance to defibrillation\n·\nHaemodynamic:\no\nVasoconstriction -> ↑SVR and\n↑PVR\no\nIf shivering: ↑metabolic rate ->\n↑venous return -> ↑cardiac\noutput\no\nIf paralysed: the opposite\nRespiratory\n·\nRespiratory depression:\no\nMainly premature neonates\no\n↓RR\no\n↓Brainstem sensitivity to\nCO\n2\n·\nReduced oxygenation (and\n↑SvO\n2\n)\no\n↓Metabolic rate ->\n↓VO\n2\no\nLeft shift OHDC -> ↓tissue uptake\nNeurological\n·\nPeripheral:\no\nShivering (if not paralysed)\no\nHyporeflexia\n·\nCentral:\no\n↓Metabolic rate = cerebral protection\no\n↓Seizures\no\n↓MAC, ↓propofol\nCp\n50\no\n↓GCS (confusion) if severe\nRenal\n·\n↓ADH synthesis -> cold\ndiuresis\nHaematological\n·\n↑Viscosity ->\n↑afterload\n·\nCoagulopathy:\no\n<35\n°\nC platelet dysfunction\no\n<33\n°\nC factor dysfunction\nImmunological\n·\n↓WBC activity ->\n↑susceptibility to infection (if\n<36\n°\nC)\nCompensation:\nBehavioural\nMediated by hypothalamus and cortex, absent\nunder GA:\n·\nShelter\n·\nInsulation\n·\nMotor activity -> ↑metabolic\nrate\nAutonomic\nMediated by hypothalamus, impaired under\nGA:\n·\nPeripheral vasoconstriction ->\n↓skin blood flow 3x\n·\nShivering -> ↑metabolic rate\n2-3x\n·\nBrown fat metabolism (neonates only)\nFeedback welcome at\nketaminenightmares@gmail.com",
